      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **LGTM with minor suggestions** — See inline comments for optional improvements. [[trajectory](go/traj/a7ac2075-bb1d-4eac-ae77-5c926b4e2132)]\n\n### Review Summary\n\n*   **Functionality:** The patch correctly updates the `PANIC_REG_LIST` macro for RISC-V to use `M_GPR` instead of `M` for general-purpose registers (`a0-a7`, `t0-t6`). It appropriately preserves `ra` by continuing to use `M`. This ensures `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_PANIC_STRIP_GPR` behaves correctly as it does on Cortex-M.\n*   **Security:** This improves privacy/security on RISC-V devices by stripping potentially sensitive data from GPRs when `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_PANIC_STRIP_GPR` is enabled.\n*   **Style:** The changes align perfectly with the existing patterns in the codebase for panic register definitions.\n*   **Testing \u0026 Test Coverage:** The patch modifies `zephyr/test/hwtest/src/panic.c` to remove `ra` from `expected_regs` so the test does not incorrectly fail when GPR stripping is enabled. However, this entirely removes test coverage for `ra`. I have left an inline comment suggesting a way to explicitly verify that `ra` retains its value and is not accidentally stripped.\n*   **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** The CL is appropriately scoped to this specific bug fix and test enablement.\n*   **Overall Quality:** Excellent, simple, and straightforward fix for a clear issue.\n\nTAG\u003dagy",
