      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] By removing `ra` from `expected_regs`, we are no longer verifying that `ra` is correctly saved during a panic. More importantly, we lose the test coverage to ensure that `ra` is *preserved* (not stripped) when `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_PANIC_STRIP_GPR` is enabled.\n\nSince `ra` uses `M` instead of `M_GPR` (which is correct), it should retain its original value. Consider adding an explicit assertion for `ra` outside of the `expected_regs` loop in `test_panic_data()` to maintain this coverage:\n\n```c\n\tif (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_RISCV)) {\n\t\t/* ra should never be stripped */\n\t\tzassert_equal(0xecec0010, pdata-\u003eriscv.regs[29]);\n\t}\n```",
